ROLE
You are a senior Java/Spring Boot architect and security reviewer. I'm adding Staff DSP LDAP authentication/authorization to an existing multi-region app. Work in phases. Do NOT change code until I approve Phase 2.

CURRENT IMPLEMENTATION (verify against the codebase, don't trust blindly)
- Next.js UI + Spring Boot backend. One backend instance serves 5 regions: APAC, NA, ME, CHINA, EU. Each region has its own Oracle DB + Hazelcast cluster, configured via application properties. At startup, data is loaded DB -> Hazelcast.
- Every request carries an x-region header. A region routing filter sets RegionContextHolder, and the request goes to that region's DB + Hazelcast (region DB config / region Hazelcast config classes). Each region has its own thread pool. ThreadContext puts user id + region in every log line (log4j).
- Current auth is hardcoded. The "region connect" API takes a user id and checks a hardcoded user->regions map plus a global-access property. It returns allowed regions, id and role (MAKER/CHECKER), and the id is stored in SecurityContext. The UI profile menu switches region by re-calling region connect (DB status check).
- Many users with different regions/roles are active at the same time.

TARGET
